On Tue, 28 Apr 1998, Jure Simsic wrote:

> Does anybody know how to disable core dumps on DU4?
> Should one do it with ulimit and what should be a sensible setting?

This command will limit core files to 0, effectively disabling them:
	ulimit -Sc 0
What it does is set the soft limit for core files, which is like a quota,
to 0.  If you put this command in the /etc/profile file then it will
affect every user who logs in, which is probably what you want.

You can use ulimit to help eliminate core dumps but every now and then
they'll still pop up.  I developed a cron script that finds and removes
core files from users directories to help counteract this behavior.

