mirko_vukovic@notes.mrc.sony.com wrote:

> questions:
> when I add the third rz29 to the lsm group and volume, how do I expand the
> volume size to its maximum
> size (other then calculating it and setting it manually)?
>
> how do I expand the size of the domain and file system mounted on that volume
> to absorb the new space?  last time, I had to remove it and then re-install it
> again.

if you choose to add at the lsm level :

-1- You don't use striping : you'll use volassist growby (or growto). In this case
you'll have to backup your file system, re-create advfs domain and filesets, and
then restore after the lsm config update. IMHO, in this case don't use lsm, use
only advfs multi-volume capability, it is much smarter, you can grow or shrink
online and get rid of lsm. (see point 3).

-2- You use striping : you'll backup your data and you'll re-create a totally new
stripe set with 3 subdisk. Then re-create advfs domain and filesets, and then
restore. that is the best performance configuration

-3- You could also use multi-volume capability of advfs, in this case just use
addvol command from advfs (you need advfs-utility license). If you have big files
(which seems to be the case), and if you want good numbers, you can force a file
to be striped. Have a look at "stripe" command, it's a *very* good performer.

Good luck
--
