On Fri, 17 Apr 1998 15:51:19 GMT, Jeffrey Sick <wolfanger@wolfcrews.com> 
wrote:

>I figured out a way to add hundreds of users at a time to a DEC UNIX
>4.0D / C2 server at a time using a script but I can't find a way of
>the password being added as well. Does anyone know of a method of
>doing this?

You may use this Perl subroutine:

# $pwd must be the uncrypted password

$cryptpwd=crypt($pwd,$salt);

sub saltchar {
    $rc=rand(62);
    if ($rc<25) { $rc+=65; }     #  0-24 goes   A-Z
    elsif ($rc<50) { $rc+=72; }  # 25-49 goes   a-z
    else { $rc-=4; }             # 50-61 goes ./0-9
    $rc;
}
					
Hope this helps,
Erik
