Hi everybody.

Recently, I've been playing with DNS, mail and other things that are
affected by DNS. Today I became aware of another one.

When I tried to start dtadvfs (or dxadvfs) I was placed in a "Choose
host" dialog box. When I tried to cennect to my machine (Quark), I was
rejected. My machine is a DNS server for the domain. I ran into similar
behavior when I tried to connect from another machine (duled) to it's
local advfsd. Also I couldn't connect from duled to Qaurk's advfsd.

I have placed both hosts in /usr/opt/advfsd/.../hosts.allow file and
restarted advfsd. No change in behavior.

I have successfully connected from duled (DNS client) to advfsd on miraz
(no DNS).

Facts/impressions:
------------------

1. Hosts: Quark - DNS server
          duled - DNS client
          miraz - no DNS

2. DNS works like it should, for Quark and duled.

3. Mail works like it should, for DNS machines.

4. dxhosts (host access for X windows) works.

5. DTAdvFS starts, but cannot connect to advfsd on local host
   or on other host with DNS.

6. The same program connects to advfsd on a machine with no DNS.

7. /usr/opt/advfs/log/... shows: "AUDIT CHECK FAILED ..." 
   for every attempt I made to connect to advfsd with DNS.

----------------------------------------------------------------

What am I missing here?
I'll keep playing with the problem, but would appreciate any insight on
the problem.

TYIA,
Nix.





