Hi,

You may have tried this.
When we were having a single Alpha box for evaluation,
we had a hard time convincing dtadvfs to connect to local host.
The Digital guy finally edited /etc/svc.conf and changed
hosts lookup order from "bind,local" to "local,bind".

That allowed dtadvfs to talk to the localhost, because
the evaluation box has a hostname (A) they chose, a valid
IP address i.j.k.l in our IP space,
but the same IP address is registered on our DNS as hostname B.
A != B. As I said it was for evaluation and everything was not
set up as it should in production.

Mingzuo



