snake@severn.office.aol.com (Joel K. Gallun) writes:

> 
> Marco Alberoni <alberoni@sasib18.sasibrlw.bo.nettuno.it> writes:
> 
> > I work on a digital workstation. Tools on the machine like
> > prof or gprof don't permit to profile such kind of processes.
> > Which kind of tool (if existing) can I use?
> 
> man atom
--

ATOM won't do it - he's dynamically loading the modules.
Atom can handles shared libraries, but not 'dlopen' modules.

You might be able to use DCPI - I think the latest version supports
dlopen-loaded code. Do a search for 'DCPI' or go to the research
sub-pages of www.digital.com, and go to DEC-WRL or DEC-SRC web pages.


-- 
Dirk Grunwald                 Assoc. Prof, Univ. of Colorado at Boulder



