Organization: Digital Equipment Corp., Software Partners Engineering
Mime-Version: 1.0
Reply-To: Jeff.Donsbach@digital.com
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


You are probably hitting the default data segment limit for a process.

In your C Shell before running your program, say "unlimit datasize".
This will allow your data segment to grow up to 1GB. For more than that,
you need to change some kernel parameters and reboot.

-Jeff

