Alpha design and fabrication as a competition to Merced? Merced will
have few things going for it that Alpha doesn't, except the
manufactoring capabaility of Intel. Both have to accomidate IA32
applications, either via fx!32 (which will be embedded in the NT5
kernel) or via on-the-fly binary translation (i.e., x86->VLIW, much
like DAISY from IBM).

