"Mark R. Bowyer" <Mark.Bowyer@uk.sun.com> writes:
> Paul Eggert wrote:
> >I need the "From:" line to be set
> >every time, consistently and automatically, the same way that I can set
> >it with most other email clients.
>"Most other email clients" I assume means PC ones.

No, it means most other email clients period.  This includes email
clients on Solaris.  It's not just Netscape; it's also pine, Emacs
RMAIL, and Gnus, just to take the first three I thought of.

(What email clients do _you_ use?  :-)

But anyway, a nice Sun engineer (whose name I won't reveal since he
probably already gets too much email as it is) told me how to get what
I want with dtmail.  If you want your From: line to say `From: My Name
<myname@my.domain.name>' then add the following to $HOME/.mailrc:

	set sentmailusername="myname"
	set sentmailhostname="my.domain.name"
	set mypersonalname="My Name"

and then restart dtmail.  This requires Solaris 2.6 or later.

This is a bit awkward, as there's no way to futz with these variables
in the Solaris 2.6 GUI, and the variables are not documented; but it
does what I want; thanks!



