   how much time do i need to update from Digital Unix 4.0b to 4.0d?
   (Server, Workstations).
   What is the best way to perform such a update?

Very depandant on the speed of the CDplayer.
I'd guess about 2 hrs with a 2x. Just use /sbin/installupdate

Not much different between server or workstation, really.
(Diff in my eyes: A server keeps disk for userdata heavilly exported)

The big problem is the recommended new partitionsize on /, changing
from 64 to 128MB. Not without reason. (Hint: /tmp resides on /)
According to installupdate I had 172 bytes(!) to little and had to
restart the whole operation after being into the unix-shell and did
some rm.

Full installation - postinstallation (sitespecific) task was 30 mins
with a 24x on a pws433au, incl 10 minutes before the about 75 sets was
copied in.

So I guess I will reinstall and change the partition on the root disk
also used for swap and /usr,/var in most cases.

Remember to same /etc and especially /etc/fdmns and underlying!

