rob@sheridanc.on.ca (Rob Naccarato) writes:

>Under DEC Unix 4.0D when using the pcnfsd daemon, is it
>possible to report to pc clients different sizes of partitions
>different from the actual size?

>I ask this because I'm sick and tired of maintaining 150+
>2 GB partitions to satisfy the DOS clients.

I believe this is not a PCNFS issue, but a NFS issue.  PCs that support
only NFS V2 will have problems with partitions bigger than 2GB.  (But
they might be minor, I don't have much NFS on PC experience.)  NFS V3
is what introduced support for > 2GB file systems.  I believe pcnfsd just
maps username/password into uid/gid and doesn't concern itself about
FS size.
