goyal@geocities.com wrote:
> 
> I just inherited a Digital DEC 3000 with no manuals or docs....When I boot up
> the system, it comes up with Alpha AXP on the bottom left corner and DEC OSF/1
> prompt on the other side of the screen.....My questions is - what is Alpha
> AXP and how different it is from DEC OSF/1??? Is it like UNIX operating
> system?? What is OSF/1?? Sorry for my ignorance...Any help is welcome!

Alpha AXP 21164 is a microprocessor used in DEC Alpha servers and
workstations.
  It's frequency can range from 233 to 500 and more MHz
  It's a 64-bit architecture.

DEC OSF/1 is Digital's implementation of an OSF/1.
  OSF/1 is a specification of a (very) UNIX-like operating system.
  DEC OSF/1 is designed for Alpha AXP systems only.

Digital UNIX is a new version of DEC OSF/1
  Version 3.2C/D/E/F/G had almost no differences from DEC OSF/1 V3.2
  Version 4.0A/B/C is much more enhanced (has CDE, more X-based utils,
...)
  Version 4.0D comes with Netscape navigator Gold 3.04, Java Development
Kit, ...

Cheers,
Nix.





