The DEC3000 systems are among the first Alpha workstations made. the one we
have in our office is a 150Mhz 21064.

The DEC3000 series have the Turbo-Channel expansion, modern systems all use
PCI. For this reson you cannot use WindowsNT or Linux (unless it's has been
added recently). This system is still a supported system and can run, DEC
UNIX and OpenVMS. I have seen people claim there is also FreeBSD or NetBSD
unix's available (I personnaly dislike Unix in any flavour, so this
information is based on  what I've seen around here).

Laurence

