> |   Version 4.0A/B/C is much more enhanced (has CDE, more X-based utils,
> | ...)
> If you call CDE an enhancement of course... :-]

Hmmm, debatable. I like it, but there are many new concepts in it. On
the other hand, other UNIXs are starting to use it, so we finally have
something that looks like a standard. I cannot comment on wether it's a
good standard, but I think it's better than no standard at all.

