Jeffrey Sick wrote:
> 
> I figured out a way to add hundreds of users at a time to a DEC UNIX
> 4.0D / C2 server at a time using a script but I can't find a way of
> the password being added as well. Does anyone know of a method of
> doing this?

You are adding them without "adduser" command? Like using edauth
command?

Well, why not give them passwords with "passwd"? Look below.

-------------------------------------

#!/usr/bin/zsh

UNAME=$1
UPASS=$2

passwd $UNAME << END_OF_PASS
p
$UPASS
$UPASS
END_OF_PASS

-------------------------------------

That should do it. The other alternative is C programming, which you
don't wanna do.

BTW, what other steps, aside from "edauth", (or whatever) are you taking
to insure the consistancy of the C2 databases?

CU,
Nix.





