In article <353777e0.80879138@news3.buffnet.net>,
Jeffrey Sick <wolfanger@wolfcrews.com> wrote:
> Is there a way to purge retired users without turning off the C2 
> (DEC UNIX 4.0D)?
> 
> I run a script (sorta) that adds hundreds of users at a time, then
> later a similar one that deletes them all. The problem is that
> sometimes there will be some added a second time around that existed
> and were retired before and it won't add them a second time. If I turn
> off C2 before the mass retiring they go a way completely, I was hoping
> that I can do the same thing without turning odd C2 first.

Convert individual users to base security using `convuser', remove them
from the passwd file (use `userdel'), and then use `convuser -d' to clean
up the C2 database.

Tim
