Changes since 1.31:

 + Better handling of "BSD4.4" sockaddr struct's (_SOCKADDR_LEN).
 + Compiles cleanly under D-Unix 4.0b (as well as 3.2x and 4.0d)
 + New command line flag:   -c bytes   [default 64k]
   to limit the number of bytes malloc'd and copied out
   of the traced processes' address space.  For example,
   this mistake:

     struct sockaddr_in sin;
     int slen = sizeof(sin);

     fillin(sin);
     bind(sockFd, &sin, &slen);     /* should be bind(sockFd, &sin, slen); */

   passing the pointer to slen, rather than slen itself
   would cause trace to try to malloc and then read a
   very large number of bytes to decode 'sin', often
   causing trace to give up or die.

