jlaiho@ichaos.nullnet.fi (Juha Laiho) writes:

>.. isn't modifying the 'From: ' headers a task for the mail transport
>agent as opposed to the mail user agent?

First, you're assuming that the mail transport agent can be configured
to munge `From:' headers, and that it is configured correctly or the
user can cause it to be configured correctly.  These assumptions are
often false in real life.

Second, you're assuming that there is no valid reason for someone to
want a From: line that is something other than the location he sent
email from.  This assumption is also incorrect.  For example, I might
be sending email via my ISP but want return mail to be sent to my
corporate address.

The PC email client vendors figured out this sort of thing a long time
ago; dtmail will just have to catch up.



