Nikola Milutinovic <milutinn@EUnet.yu> writes:

>If your MTA cannot be configured correctly, change the MTA.

Yes, in an ideal world, one would be free to change the MTA exactly
as desired, and the MTA would always be configured correctly.
However, in the real world, I assure you that this is not the case.
Often the MTA is under control of another organization that is not
technically competent or is bureaucratically unwilling to fix things.
Also, some MTAs are not as configurable as sendmail, and for technical
or bureaucratic reasons they can't be replaced by a better MTA.

>FYI, "From:" field indicates who_sent_that_message. What you need is
>"Reply-to:" address

In an ideal world, you're correct; but in the real world, many MUAs
ignore or botch handling of Reply-To, and the Reply-To line can get
lost or munged when your message gets quoted; so it's important to be
able to set `From:' as well.



