In article <01bd5e62$73bfaf70$2415989e@wsmain>, "dave herdman"
<dherdman@osil.demon.co.uk> wrote:

>I have a fairly big Oracle database (250Gig) on an 8400 with 4 x HSZ50. I
>have set the system up so that the database tablespace files (approx 6GB
>each) are ADVFS striped accross the 4 HSZs thereby spreading I/O accross 4
>KZPSAs. This works fine but a recovery test reveals that vrestore seems not
>to honour the stripped attribute. (issues a warning saying it is unable to
>restore file attributes)
>
>BTW I did a proof of concept exercise on a workstation running 4.0 and
>vrestore did restore the striping just fine. Has this feature gone away in
>4.0B? 

_IF_ you have _LESS_ volumes in your recovery domain than were in the
original domain, vrestore will not stripe the file (or it may require the
domain have at  least as many volumes as were specified in the "stripe -n
xxx filename" command, I'm not sure).  If you have the same number of
volumes in the recovery domain as were in the original, then vrestore
should correctly stripe the file.

If this is not the case, then I would suggest contacting your Digital
Customer Service Center and reporting a bug.  If this is very importan to
you, then have them specify it as a level 2 IPMT.  By the way I did a quick
test using V4.0d of a striped file on a 5 volume AdvFS domain and it worked
correctly.

