Here is a sample /etc/printcap file which prints a few of our HP
printers with Jet Direct cards.  I think that the CDE setup tool can
also be used to build printcap files.  If you don't use the setup tool
you may have to manually create the directories for the lf and sd
fields.  The Jet Direct card has two queue names "raw" and "text".
See your HP printer manual for a description of the differences.  We
have had our current JetDirect printers for about 2 years, when we got
them the firmware was buggy.  I suggest checking out the HP website
for the latest firmware upgrades.

		hope this helps,

			Eric


# HP LaserJet 5M PostScript Printer 
lp0|0|lp|PostScript:\
	:lf=/usr/adm/lp0err:\
	:lp=:\
	:rm=printer.ip.number:\
	:rp=text:\
	:sd=/usr/spool/lpd0:
raw:\
	:lf=/usr/adm/lp0err:\
	:lp=:\
	:rm=printer.ip.number:\
	:rp=raw:\
	:sd=/usr/spool/lpd0:

# HP 1600CM Color PostScript Printer 
lp1|1|:Color:\
	:lf=/usr/adm/lp1err:\
	:lp=:\
	:rm=color.printer.ip.number:\
	:rp=text:\
	:sd=/usr/spool/lpd1:

