> :: (wrong) name for the product set.  Product sets begin with the
> :: string "CXL" and are:
> ::
> :: CXLLIBA410           installed  DEC C++ Class Archive Libraries
> :: CXLSHRDA410          installed  DEC C++ Class Shared Libraries
> ::
> ::   Step two is to fix the (broken) installation script on the floppy
> :: disk.  I copied the floppy disk's contents to /tmp and worked there.
> :: This has to be done because the install script still checks for
> :: the old name of the C++ libraries; "CXX" instead of "CXL".
> ::
> ::   Go into the "instctrl" directory and edit SWXCRMGR111.scp, find
> :: the line that says:
> ::
> ::     STL_DepEval   CXXSHRDA??? || {
> ::
> :: and change it to:
> ::
> ::     STL_DepEval   CXLSHRDA??? || {
> ::
> ::   At this point, setld is happy because the C++ libraries are
> :: installed and it is checking for the right name.
> --

The libraries changed their names because libcxx.so is now a required
piece of the base operating system.  This should be in the release 
notes.

Anyway, I don't know what pieces of the C++ Class Libraries the
SWXCRMGR111 kit needs but CXLLIBA4xx contains the .a versions of 
libcxx.a/libtask.a and libcomplex.a.  
CXLSHRDA4xx contains only libtask.so and libcomplex.so.

If the SWX utility does not require libtask or libcomplex, or the .a
files, the scp portion of it could just check for OSFBASE4?? which
will have libcxx.so in it.

Since I'm the PL for the C++ Class Libraries, thats about as close to
an official response as you are going to get :-)

We realized these type of issues would occur when library subset names
were changed but because of the requirement of the libcxx.so being
part of the base OS, we had little choice.

Brian J. McCarthy
