Hi

Our local (class C) network consists of 4 subnets with one machine (DEC
Workstation running digital UNIX 4.0c) connected to all nets and
configured as a router.

I would like to get IP broadcast packets originating from one subnet to
be sent into (at least) one other subnet and interpreted here as what
they are - broadcast messages (for the purpose of getting 'rwhod' to
work network-wide, for instance).

Setting the broadcast address alike for all machines obviously is not
possible since the broadcast address depends on the subnet mask.

I guess it could be accomplished through some kind of filtering done by
the router. Is this correct ? Could someone enlighten me, how ?

Kay

