At first sight, there are indeed few things you can do with Word 97 that you
couldn't with Wordperfect 5.1 for DOS. However, if you think about it, it
soon becomes apparent that Word 97 is much more powerful, and has many more
features, Now, I agree that most of them are not used by most users, but
that still does not mean they aren't worth having. Consider just two simple
examples: answer wizard/tip wizard- these genuinely make it much easier for
novice users, and even veterans occasionally get something out of them. At
the other end of the spectrum, take Wordbasic/VBA- only experts will use
this, but it renders previously impossible tasks simple. You also have to
accept that a Windows program has much higher overheads than a DOS program,
but this does bring ease of use as well.

Already, we are seeing voice dictation coming in- this will one day be
standard, and then we will need all the CPU cycles we can get.






