We're running DEC Unix 4.0D on an Alpha 4000.  I have printers which
are attached to a Synoptics terminal server.  I want to set up print
queues to those printers.  I tried the tcp/ip print setup as outlined
in the System Admistrators Guide.  It works, but as indicated in the
guide, we have problems with lost carriage returns using the lpf print
filter.  Synoptics provides a shell script and filter for their system
but it is not clear to me how I would implement this on the DEC system.
I am guessing I would setup attributes in the printcap files as follows:

citsysptr|lp0:\
:af=/usr/adm/lpacct:\
:ct=tcp:\
:if=/usr/lbin/ts3395.model:\ #This is the script provided by Synoptics.
:lf=/usr/adm/lperr:\
:lp=/dev/null:\
:mc#20:\
:mx#0:\
:of=/usr/lbin/lpf:\
:pl#66:\
:pw#80:\
:rw:\
:sd=/usr/spool/lpd:\
:xf=/usr/lbin/xf:

If you have any information on this I would greatly appreciate it.
Thanks,
Karl
