Organization: University of Wisconsin, Madison
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


We have observed a bug in Digital UNIX 4.0D that can lead to erroneous
numerical results in Fortran programs.  It is independent of machine
type (have observed it on both Alpha 500/533 and 255/300 machines). 
Have no idea what the bug is, but reinstalling 4.0B makes the problem go
away; the same Fortran libraries were used to test this.

We first noticed the problem when the DXML V3.3 (parallel library) IVP
would not run upon installation of the set.  Further checks with
established Fortran code results then revealed the numerical
inconsistencies.

I tried this morning to report the bug to DEC, but could not breach
their incredible front-end bureaucratic wall; since we don't pay for
software support, they wouldn't let me speak to anyone in OS development
directly.  And the first person even tried to make us do a pay-per-call
to report the problem.  I ended up describing the problem to some
Unit-Level Manager in a Chicago office, who apparently wrote down what I
described, to be forwarded to the OS guys, but then dictated it back
partly wrong.

A 4.0D OS patch appeared yesterday on the DEC public ftp site.  There
don't seem to be any appropriate patches, but we haven't tried it out
yet.

Anyone else run into this feature?

Dave Rainwater
U. of Wisconsin - physics - phenomenology



