  I'm not sure if this is the best group to send this message to, but didn't
see any comp.mail groups that looked very relevant...
  Our center is in the process of installing a firewall.  One of the
impacts on users will be that incoming e-mail will only go through a central
post office machine with addresses of the form  user@larc.nasa.gov, rather
than to individual workstations with addresses like user2@wkst1.larc.nasa.gov
(the post office username and that on the individual workstations are not
necessarily identical).
  As a result, our outgoing e-mail needs to appear to come from the
post office machine.  Using mutt or elm, it's relatively easy to modify the
"From:" field or add a "Reply-to:" field in the start-up options file.  
Some, however, use the dtmail e-mail client.  I'm not very familiar with 
this software, but I've found no easy way to modify the "From:" field 
using dtmail.  In the mail options window, you can add a "Reply-to:" field, 
but it requires an effort to get this field into each message sent out.
  Is there a simply way of modifying the From: field or adding a Reply-to:
field in dtmail without requiring the end-user to add extra fields each
time they want to send a message?
  Thanks.

