..ds n 5
..SH NAME
\fBcdrom\fR - mounts or unmounts ISO-cdrom to /cdrom
..SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcdrom\fR
..br
..SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcdrom\fR lets a user mount an ISO-cdrom on /cdrom. If the CDROM-drive is 
currently used by another user, you will be informed and no attempt to mount 
the CDROM will de made. To unmount the CDROM enter \fBcdrom\fR again. If 
the CDROM contains Rockridge extensions, these will be used. 
..SH SEE ALSO
\fBmount\fR(8), \fBcdfs\fR(4)
