Hi folks

re the various replies offering advice on different hardware setups:-

I am using RAID 0+1 volumes on the HSZ50s.Each HSZ is on its own KZPSA.
Each of the Oracle ADVFS filesets are made up of 4 RAID volumes (1 on
each HSZ). The Oracle tablespace files 6GB+ are FILE LEVEL striped using
ADVFS file stripe facility.

Why?

Because this speads database I/O out across all the available hardware
in a reasonably even manner ie no real hardware hotspots { the
distribution and access of the data is fairly even across the tables) 

Yes there are other ways of doing this LSM being one. 

The issue I am raising is that ADVFS striping works fine as initially
set up but when I restore using vrestore (to exactly the same hardware
and ADVFS set up) vrestore does not honour the stripe attributes



